    {
      "id": "claim_105cc541a4ca495ca2142af7e470579f",
      "statement": "Revocation is lazy: removing a collaborator severs only the edges granting them access and revoking a link sets a revoked flag, nothing cascades, and users who lose their only path become unreachable and are denied at open() time; because the graph is never destructively pruned, revocation is reversible.",
